 and the text 'less than x'.  Similarly, a right-pointing arrow on the line=
 connecting 'X' to the right subtree indicates values greater than 'X' are =
contained within the purple, right subtree labeled 'right subtree' and the =
text 'greater than x'. To the right, the text 'inorder traversal:' describe=
s the traversal order as 'left subtree =E2=86=92 x =E2=86=92 right subtree'=
, indicating that in an inorder traversal, the left subtree is visited firs=
t, followed by the root node 'X', and finally the right subtree." loading=
=3D"lazy" width=3D"546" height=3D"160" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" s=
